  "articleBody": "Slippery spots in the kitchen are no joke, right? You're rushing around, maybe a little water or grease gets on the floor, and suddenly you've got a slip hazard. The first thing you've gotta do is clean up spills immediately. Don't leave them sitting! Make sure the floor's totally dry before anyone walks on it again. For wet or greasy areas, think about flooring that's designed to be safer in those conditions. And hey, those loose mats? They can be just as bad as a spill. Look for slip-resistant mats with backing that actually stays put. If you're constantly battling slippery spots, or if you've got drainage issues creating puddles, it might be time to get a pro involved. HH Remodeling LLC can take a look and help you figure out a more permanent solution to keep your kitchen safe and sound. Give us a call at 303-505-0866 to chat about it.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
}